    "verseCount": 8,
    "content": "<p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"1\" data-sid=\"PSA 129:1\" class=\"v\">1</span>Out of the depths I have cried to thee, O Lord:</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"2\" data-sid=\"PSA 129:2\" class=\"v\">2</span>Lord, hear my voice. Let thy ears be attentive to the voice of my supplication.</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"3\" data-sid=\"PSA 129:3\" class=\"v\">3</span>If thou, O Lord, wilt mark iniquities: Lord, who shall stand it.</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"4\" data-sid=\"PSA 129:4\" class=\"v\">4</span>For with thee there is merciful forgiveness: and by reason of thy law, I have waited for thee, O Lord. My soul hath relied on his word:</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"5\" data-sid=\"PSA 129:5\" class=\"v\">5</span>My soul hath hoped in the Lord.</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"6\" data-sid=\"PSA 129:6\" class=\"v\">6</span>From the morning watch even until night, let Israel hope in the Lord.</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"7\" data-sid=\"PSA 129:7\" class=\"v\">7</span>Because with the Lord there is mercy: and with him plentiful redemption.</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"8\" data-sid=\"PSA 129:8\" class=\"v\">8</span>And he shall redeem Israel from all his iniquities.</p>",
